    "narrative": "Our offensive ceiling today is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Kyle Tucker** (69.85), who present the most compelling profiles against the right-handed arms of Sasaki and Buehler, respectively. **Jackson Merrill** benefits significantly from a favorable park environment and a slow-delivery opposing starter, maximizing his stolen base potential, while **Kyle Tucker** remains our most bankable asset in standard scoring formats. **Nasim Nunez** (68.24) is a sneaky high-floor play today; while he occupies the 8-hole, his matchup against Rogers, Tr, combined with his elite sprint speed and the pitcher\u2019s glacial pace to the plate, makes him a priority start for us in the scarcity-driven SB category. **Josh Jung** (66.06) also warrants mention as a top-tier option, leveraging a solid park factor and a favorable matchup against a left-handed pitcher to slot firmly into our utility spot.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (53.42) on the bench despite his reputation. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** possesses a high raw base projection, he is currently being squeezed out by the efficiency of **Coby Mayo** (58.48) and **Gunnar Henderson** (59.45). Despite the latter two facing the tougher Alvarez (3.59 xERA), the situational adjustments for park factors and, in **Gunnar Henderson**'s case, his aggressive top-of-the-order usage, ultimately provided higher projected efficiency scores. **Drake Baldwin** (47.24) and **Cole Carrigg** (56.22) remain marginal starts, but we will keep a close eye on weather developments, as any sudden shift in park conditions could necessitate a pivot to **Sam Antonacci** (52.37) or **Brayan Rocchio** (50.95), both of whom are ready to be deployed should an injury or lineup change trigger a late-afternoon scratch.",
